What:           /sys/class/leds/vibrator/activate
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        linux-leds@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Writing a nonzero value starts a pulse for the configured
                duration. Writing zero stops it and cancels pending timer
                work. Reading reports whether the bridge is running.

What:           /sys/class/leds/vibrator/duration
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        linux-leds@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Configured pulse duration in milliseconds, clamped to 60000.
                This is not a remaining-time counter.

What:           /sys/class/leds/vibrator/state
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        linux-leds@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Boolean configuration latch for the MediaTek vibrator HAL.
                Writing this attribute does not start or stop the bridge.
                It is not cleared on cancellation or expiry; read activate
                to determine whether the bridge is running.
